<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: the frame cookie MSVC stores on the stack is no
    argument of a call made below it.

    Issue:      kuna GH-1593 - the /GS cookie pushed in an SEH prologue
                (`mov eax,[___security_cookie]; xor eax,esp; push eax`) is
                printed as a stack argument of calls in the body.
    Stage:      P4 calls - checkInputTrialUse's stack trials
                (`p4_calls/kuna_stackcookie.rs`, `funcdata_callsite.rs`).

    stackcookie_pe_i386.exe (clean-room, source and recipe in
    stackcookie_pe_i386.s): gsseh (0x401000) pushes the cookie below an SEH
    frame and calls lookup("NAME") through a pointer, cleaning up after it;
    gsthis (0x401050) calls a method on this+8 with no stack argument under
    the same frame; gsebp (0x401090) keeps the cookie at [ebp-4] and checks it
    before returning. No call takes the cookie (#1-#3), and the check still
    gets it in ECX (#4).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/stackcookie_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x401000 as gsseh</com>
  <com>load function gsseh</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x401050 as gsthis</com>
  <com>load function gsthis</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x401090 as gsebp</com>
  <com>load function gsebp</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="STACKCOOKIE #1: the call under an SEH frame takes only its pushed name" min="1" max="1">= \(\*dat_403004\)\(s_40301c\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="STACKCOOKIE #2: the method under an SEH frame takes only this" min="1" max="1">^  sub_4010c0\(a0 \+ 8\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="STACKCOOKIE #3: the call in an EBP frame takes only its argument" min="1" max="1">\(\*dat_403008\)\(a0\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="STACKCOOKIE #4: the epilogue check still receives the cookie in ECX" min="1" max="1">sub_4010f0\(v[0-9]+ \^ \(uint4\)&amp;Stack</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
